url: 'https://github.com/Sukhmangill977/gc-ir-reference'
date-released: '2026-09-12'
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation and empirical artifact for a deterministic method that
  compiles approved AI governance assessments into enforceable runtime predicates.
  Implements the governed semantic refinement relation Psi_K closed by a signed
  judgment record, the GC-IR record family with total risk disposition, the
  deterministic compiler Phi with RFC 8785 canonicalization and SHA-256 bundle
  hashing, authority closure against an approved action matrix, the consequence-class
  gate coverage rule, a separately signed lifecycle registry, and a temporally valid
  traceability model with ten canonical audit queries. v1.1.0 adds a nine-Approved-
  Control-Specification Case B (twelve predicates total; the historical six-
  specification Case B remains reported as unchanged baseline evidence) and a third
  case, Case C, exercising schema v1.1 mechanisms. Ships three hash-pinned worked
  cases, a governance provenance verifier, a two-axis authorization/release
  injection harness, an adversarial corpus, property-based tests, and the
  reportable campaign under the public prospective scientific freeze
  preregister-tier0-v4.1.
keywords:
  - AI governance
  - risk register
  - policy compilation
  - semantic refinement
  - runtime enforcement
  - agentic AI
  - model risk management
  - non-compensatory aggregation
  - traceability
  - RFC 8785
  - JSON canonicalization
  - reproducibility
references:
